#
# JIT inline directives for jinfer's hot Vector API helpers.
#
# These small methods return / consume jdk.incubator.vector FloatVector values. When the JIT does NOT inline
# them into their hot loop, the vector escapes the method boundary and is boxed (a FloatVector object + its
# backing float[] are allocated per call) instead of scalar-replaced into a SIMD register. On a strong inliner
# (Oracle GraalVM) this happens automatically; weaker inliners (GraalVM CE, plain C2 under budget pressure)
# need the hint. Forcing the inline makes the whole loop allocation-free — measured +~45% prefill on GraalVM CE.
#
# Use with:  -XX:CompileCommandFile=<path>/hotspot_compiler
# Format:    one "inline <class-with-slashes>.<method>" per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Stock C2 alternative (no per-method list): -XX:InlineSmallCode=1000000 alone recovers the same
# prefill (741 vs 756 t/s, LFM 8B Q4_K_M pp512; no-flags baseline 516). Root cause: the vector-
# returning helpers hit compile thresholds before their callers (leaf methods run 64x more), their
# standalone nmethods are bloated by boxing, and C2 then refuses to inline them ("already compiled
# into a big method" / "callee uses too much stack") - raising the size heuristics
# (FreqInlineSize/MaxInlineSize) does nothing because this check fires first. Decode needs no
# flags at all: MatMul routes the C2-hostile k-quant dots to JAM.
#
# NOTE: Convert.f16ToF32Vector is deliberately NOT force-inlined: loadF16 (below) is, and
# Graal inlines the tiny converter into it naturally. Force-inlining the converter AT EVERY CALL
# SITE on top of the already-forced qkTile/pvTile bodies blew Graal's compilation units in qwen35's
# hybrid attention layers - measured 2.0x SLOWER prefill on Oracle GraalVM 25.1 (863 vs 1776 t/s,
# Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0). Bisect: the regression needs BOTH this line and the FlashAttention lines.
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/Ops.siluVec
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/Ops.tanhVec
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.loadF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.loadF16
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.accumulate
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.qkTile
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.qkTile64F32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.qkTileWideF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.qkRowF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.pvTile
# the bodies pvTile dispatches to (per element type): inlining the dispatcher alone still leaves
# a vector-crossing boundary
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.pvTileF16
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.pvTileF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.normalize
